    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Step 1: Mobile-First Design"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "As shown in the previous page, the design of the navbar for small devices (e.g., phones, tablets) is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Responsive Navbar for Small Devices",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "You can start by creating the base CSS rules for mobile devices up to 600px wide."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<body>\n2    <nav class=\"navbar\">\n3        <div class=\"logo\">MySite</div>\n4        <ul class=\"nav-links\">\n5            <li><a href=\"#\">Home</a></li>\n6            <li><a href=\"#\">About</a></li>\n7            <li><a href=\"#\">Services</a></li>\n8            <li><a href=\"#\">Contact</a></li>\n9        </ul>\n10        <div class=\"icon\">☰</div>\n11    </nav>\n12</body>"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "css",
      "content": "1* {\n2    margin: 0;\n3    padding: 0;\n4    box-sizing: border-box;\n5}\n6\n7body {\n8    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n9    color: #333;\n10}\n11\n12.navbar {\n13    display: flex;\n14    justify-content: space-between;\n15    padding: 1rem;\n16    background: black;\n17}\n18\n19.logo {\n20    font-size: 1.5rem;\n21    font-weight: bold;\n22    color: white;\n23}\n24\n25.nav-links {\n26    /* Makes nav-links hidden */\n27    display: none;\n28}\n29\n30.icon {\n31    color: white;\n32    font-size: 1.5rem;\n33}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, we have simply added an extra element:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "css",
      "content": "<div class=\"icon\">☰</div>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The code above creates the hamburger menu, which we will display on smaller screens instead of a full navbar."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Now, let's lay out the CSS rules for medium devices."
    },
